# Package Feature Module Structure

## Goal

Each **package module** (e.g. a feature under `Client/packages/features/<name>/`) must follow a single, enforced layout. Only the following direct children are allowed.

## Allowed Structure

Under `packages/features/<featureName>/` (and any other package scope that adopts this convention), the **only** allowed direct children are:

| Item | Purpose |
|------|--------|
| **`api/`** | Network requests and endpoint definitions |
| **`components/`** | UI elements specific to this feature |
| **`hooks/`** | Custom React hooks |
| **`store/`** | Local state management |
| **`types/`** | TypeScript interfaces and models |
| **`utils/`** | Pure helper functions |
| **`index.ts`** (or `index.tsx` / `index.js`) | The public API (barrel file) |

No other files or folders may exist at the module root. Place new code in the appropriate allowed folder.

## Example

```
packages/features/saved/
├── api/          # Network requests and endpoint definitions
├── components/   # UI elements specific to this feature
├── hooks/        # Custom React hooks
├── store/        # Local state management
├── types/        # TypeScript interfaces and models
├── utils/        # Pure helper functions
└── index.ts      # The public API (barrel file)
```

## Enforcement

- **ESLint:** Rule `silverkey/package-module-allowed-children` runs on `packages/features/**` and reports any file or folder that is not one of the allowed children.
- **Scope:** By default the rule applies to `packages/features/`. Optionally configurable for other package roots via rule options (`scopeDir`, `allowedDirs`, `allowedRootFiles`).

